The legacy mod {{c|mod|Nearby Allies have +1 Fortification}} is a mod that acts as a description of the unique item aura but actually does nothing (the aura is granted by a [[Modifier:NearbyAlliesHaveFortifyUnique~~1~~|separate hidden mod]]), the item's aura still grants +10 Fortification regardless of if it is the current variant or legacy, unless it is pre-3.6 variants that do not even have the {{c|mod|Nearby Allies have +1 Fortification}} mod.

According to datamined data, the pre-3.6 legacy Kingmaker actually has a larger aura radius (5 meter verse 3 meter) for granting Culling Strike and IIR to allies,{{efn|name=legacymod}} which match the measurements done by redditor theuberelite.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.reddit.com/r/pathofexile/comments/b34qtq/psa_kingmakers_aura_radius_was_nerfed_to_about/|title=PSA: Kingmaker's aura radius was nerfed to about half the value that it used to have.|date=March 19, 2019|accessdate=May 21, 2023|publisher=Reddit}}</ref> This is despite the buff using the same status icon for both current and pre-3.6 legacy variant buffs; the status icon comes from a buff with internal id: "increased_item_rarity_aura", with the fortification (id: kingmaker_fortify_aura), crit multi (id: critical_strike_multiplier_aura) and culling strike (id: culling_strike_aura) actually coded as separate hidden buffs without status icons. In other words, it is not a bug that the aura from a pre-3.6 legacy Kingmaker does not grant crit multi or fortification despite the status icon saying it does.

